      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Follow-up outcomes of urogenital tuberculosis with involvement of the bladder are provided for patients of the Novosibirsk regional and city hospitals. The cure was achieved in 42.1% of patients, posttuberculous cystalgia (PTC) developed in 36.8% microcystitis in 21.1% of cases. Age-related hormonal insufficiency contributes to the onset of PTC. An original technique of laser thermopuncture is detailed."},
